    title_en: "AhnLab-led Consortium Builds Generative AI and Cybersecurity System Based on N2SF for Korea Research Foundation Network",
    summary_en: "A consortium led by AhnLab aims to support the establishment of a secure system for both generative AI and network usage within the Korea Research Foundation's operational network. This project is part of the \"Korea Information Network Promotion Institute 2026 National Network Security System (N2SF) Implementation Support Project.\" The established system allows users to access certified external services without switching between operational terminal devices and network PCs. Core functionalities include user authentication, terminal validation, web page isolation, and data protection function linkage, which can block unauthorized connections and minimize the exposure of threats introduced by external web content. Furthermore, the system applies a differentiated control principle based on information classification (Confidential/Sensitive/Public), preventing information leakage through tiered transmission restrictions while still supporting the utilization of necessary business information. Participating vendors in the consortium will link their respective professional technologies to build the system, and this experience is expected to assist the future implementation and expansion of N2SF in multiple institutions.",
