    title: "大型教會遭駭：數十萬教友資料外洩，專家指出外部帳號管理與零信任機制缺失為關鍵",
    summary: "近期，大型教會成為網路攻擊的目標，導致教友個人資料和內部系統資料大規模外洩。根據安全公司 Oasis Security 的分析，駭客從海外攻擊者伺服器上發現了大量資料，包括某教會約 96 萬筆教友資訊、33 萬筆奉獻紀錄、6 萬 8000 筆電子決策文件，以及內部聊天記錄等。另一教會也損失了包含 89,000 名教友的個人資料系統。專家指出，此次事件的根本原因包括外部委託服務帳號管理不善，以及內部網路缺乏細分和零信任（Zero Trust）的存取控制。由於教會的資料庫（教友名單、奉獻、人事系統、內部通訊）常在單一網路中交聯，攻擊者一旦突破，便能迅速掌握所有系統。此外，攻擊過程中還利用了 AI 輔助的自動化技術進行資料探勘。為防止類似事件，建議教會應建立媲美中型企業的專業安全體系，指定資訊保護最高主管（CISO），並加強與專業安全廠商的合作，同時提升教職員和教友的防範意識。",
    tags: ["大型教會", "個人資料外洩", "Oasis Security", "Zero Trust", "CISO", "網路安全"],
    title_en: "Large Church Hacked: Hundreds of Thousands of Member Records Leaked; Experts Point to Weak External Account Management and Lack of Zero Trust as Key Issues",
    summary_en: "Recently, large churches have become targets of cyberattacks, leading to the massive leakage of member personal data and internal system information. According to an analysis by security firm Oasis Security, hackers discovered a large volume of data on an overseas attacker server, including approximately 960,000 member records, 330,000 donation records, 68,000 electronic decision documents, and internal chat logs from one church. Another church also suffered a personal data system loss affecting 89,000 members. Experts point out that the root causes of these incidents include poor management of external outsourced service accounts and a lack of network segmentation and Zero Trust access control within the internal network. Because the church's databases (member lists, donations, HR systems, internal communications) are often interconnected within a single network, attackers, once they breach the perimeter, can quickly gain access to all systems. Furthermore, the attack process utilized AI-assisted automation techniques for data reconnaissance. To prevent similar incidents, it is recommended that churches establish professional security systems comparable to those of medium-sized enterprises, appoint a Chief Information Security Officer (CISO), strengthen cooperation with professional security vendors, and raise the awareness of both staff and members regarding prevention.",
